  "notes": "Fire Tester 0.1.753b\n\nSince 0.1.752b, this release adds request-scoped queued INA baseline and display frame-pacing diagnostics. It also gives an explicit runtime cancel or output-stop priority over a queued baseline timeout; this is covered by host regression tests, not a forced physical race test. Pulse, thresholds, INA cadence, display cadence, rendering, and smoothing are unchanged.\n\nThe normal 3,174,672-byte image was installed and normal boot verified. All 776 update blocks were acknowledged in 77.11 s. Thirty-five final host suites passed against the same 1,439 production input records used for the checked build.\n\nThe first cold cartridge check passed on its first attempt: three early and three late samples, 0.8722 ohm. Both IR sensors were ready on attempt 1. A fresh capture passed all five checks: cartridge presence, cartridge quality (61%, 872 milliohm), heater NTC (23.487 C), primary IR (83 mm), and cartridge IR (61 mm). The post-capture readback showed zero faults, outputs off, and lease and radio pause at zero. Learning data remained unchanged at 64 records, generation 90, revision 31.\n\nCooler request 14 accepted three baseline pairs, then retained three loaded samples averaging 767.9 mA at 4.182 V before ending in running-phase InaStale. The failing running predicate remains unresolved; this does not establish airflow or a cooler-health pass. No thresholds were widened.\n\nSixteen settled Desktop pacing samples had median period 18,787 us, inverse-period estimate 53.2502 FPS, and median work 17,051 us. Stable 60 FPS is not proven. This bounded measure is not directly comparable to smoothed HEALTH FPS and does not establish a causal improvement.\n\nFull QA, physical phone BLE validation, and a real hosted QR/help URL remain open. No wire-repair firmware claim is made.\n",
